sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Part as Active verified PART
    participant React as RecommendedTeamsPage
    participant API as Express recommendation API
    participant Guards as Auth and own-profile guards
    participant Service as Team recommendation service
    participant Repo as Recommendation repository
    participant DB as PostgreSQL via Supabase

    Part->>React: Open Recommended teams
    React->>API: GET /api/recommendations/teams
    API->>Guards: Verify token, MFA, active PART, email, own profile
    alt Visitor, ADMIN, suspended, unverified, or another profile named
        Guards-->>React: Safe 400, 401, or 403 without profile existence
        React-->>Part: Signed-out or error state
    else Authorized own profile
        Guards->>Service: Use req.participant.id only
        Service->>DB: Load participant, profile, skills, and LFT availability
        DB-->>Service: Current participant matching inputs
        Service->>Repo: listEligibleTeamVacanciesForParticipant
        Repo->>DB: Read confirmed memberships and Pending requests
        Repo->>DB: Query Open visible vacancies and recruiting teams
        DB-->>Repo: Database-prefiltered candidates
        Repo-->>Service: Candidates and pending-request team ids
        Service->>Service: Reapply eligibility backstop
        Service->>Service: Score skills, goal, and hours with rankTeamVacancies
        Service->>Service: Rank by score, matched skills, team, and vacancy
        Service-->>API: Safe scored recommendation DTO
        API-->>React: 200 no-store
        alt Empty candidate list
            React-->>Part: Empty guidance or profile action
        else Non-empty candidate list
            React->>React: Validate rank, matchPercent, skills, and explanations
            React-->>Part: Ranked cards with match details and Apply action
        end
    end

    Note over React,Service: The live service invokes the task 155 scorer, and the task 159 contract suite verifies that the server response satisfies the React parser.
    Note over API,DB: The query is platform-wide. No event is selected, trusted, or returned, and safe DTOs omit emails, Firebase ids, membership rows, and request details.

